From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: project/JavaToolchainPlugin: use JAVA_HOME instead of fetching JDKs

The plugin auto-applies to every subproject and resolves toolchain
JDKs by shelling out to `bin/coursier java-home --jvm <ver>`.
Coursier downloads any missing JDK from cdn.azul.com /
adoptium-binaries on demand — but those tarballs are
glibc-linked, so they cannot exec on Chimera's musl libc even
if we let the download complete.

Two surgical changes:

(1) `getJavaHome` short-circuits to `$JAVA_HOME`.  cports' template
    sets this to /usr/lib/jvm/java-21-openjdk; one JDK serves all
    `javaToolchainVersion` queries since javac on JDK 21 can target
    earlier classfile versions natively.

(2) `javacOptions` switches from
        "-target", "1.8", "-source", "1.8", "-bootclasspath", <rt.jar>
    to
        "--release", javaToolchainVersion.value
    `--release N` was added in JDK 9 and is the modern equivalent
    of `-target N -source N -bootclasspath rtN.jar` — javac uses
    bundled CT signature files for the requested release, so we
    don't need a separate JDK 8 install (or its rt.jar) on disk.
    The per-subproject `javaToolchainVersion := "8"|"11"|"17"|"21"`
    overrides in build.sbt continue to work as before; "11"
    (the plugin default) and "8" are the common cases.

This produces semantically identical bytecode for the embedded
javac plugins (semanticdb-javac etc.) — they remain Java-8
binary-compatible, just compiled by JDK 21's javac in
cross-compile mode rather than JDK 8 itself.

--- a/project/JavaToolchainPlugin.scala
+++ b/project/JavaToolchainPlugin.scala
@@ -27,16 +27,13 @@
   import autoImport._
 
   override lazy val projectSettings: Seq[Def.Setting[_]] = List(
+    // PATCH (Chimera): use --release instead of -target/-source/
+    // -bootclasspath so we don't need a separate JDK 8 install.
+    // JDK 21's javac generates per-release CT signatures itself.
     javacOptions ++=
-      List(
-        "-target",
-        "1.8",
-        "-source",
-        "1.8",
-        "-bootclasspath",
-        java8Bootclasspath()
-      ),
-    (doc / javacOptions) --= List("-target", "1.8"),
+      List("--release", javaToolchainVersion.value),
+    (doc / javacOptions) --=
+      List("--release", javaToolchainVersion.value),
     (doc / javacOptions) --= bootclasspathSettings(javaToolchainVersion.value),
     (doc / javacOptions) --= List("-g"),
     javacOptions ++= bootclasspathSettings(javaToolchainVersion.value),
@@ -77,26 +74,15 @@
       version: String,
       jvmIndex: Option[String] = None
   ): File = {
-    javaHomeCache.computeIfAbsent(
-      version,
-      (v: String) => {
-        val coursier = Paths.get("bin", "coursier")
-        val index = jvmIndex
-          .toList
-          .flatMap(index => "--jvm-index" :: index :: Nil)
-        val arguments =
-          List(
-            "java",
-            "-jar",
-            coursier.toString,
-            "java-home",
-            "--jvm",
-            jvmName(v)
-          ) ++ index
-
-        new File(Process(arguments).!!.trim)
-      }
-    )
+    // PATCH (Chimera): cports' build sandbox can't run the
+    // glibc-linked Adoptium / Zulu JDK tarballs Coursier would
+    // download on demand.  Point all toolchain queries at
+    // $JAVA_HOME (set to JDK 21 by the cports template) and let
+    // javac handle cross-target compatibility via --release.
+    new File(sys.env.getOrElse("JAVA_HOME",
+      sys.error(
+        "JAVA_HOME must be set for JavaToolchainPlugin (Chimera build)"
+      )))
   }
 
